[Write file: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-edwin-iai-transcripts-v2-L1/90567ea6-3d6b-4965-b700-f047e645d34d/scratchpad/monday-reading-protocol.html]
<title>Monday Reading Protocol — Hard Science Passage</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #16181d;
    --ink-soft: #4a5160;
    --ink-faint: #767d8c;
    --rule: #d8dce4;
    --rule-soft: #e8ebf0;
    --bg: #ffffff;
    --panel: #f5f6f9;
    --accent: #1d4ed8;
    --accent-soft: #eef2ff;
    --warn-bg: #fdf6ec;
    --warn-rule: #e6d4b8;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --ink: #e8eaf0;
      --ink-soft: #a8b0c0;
      --ink-faint: #7b8494;
      --rule: #333947;
      --rule-soft: #262b36;
      --bg: #14161b;
      --panel: #1b1e26;
      --accent: #8fb0ff;
      --accent-soft: #1c2436;
      --warn-bg: #241f16;
      --warn-rule: #4a3f2a;
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme="dark"] {
    --ink: #e8eaf0; --ink-soft: #a8b0c0; --ink-faint: #7b8494;
    --rule: #333947; --rule-soft: #262b36; --bg: #14161b; --panel: #1b1e26;
    --accent: #8fb0ff; --accent-soft: #1c2436;
    --warn-bg: #241f16; --warn-rule: #4a3f2a;
  }
  :root[data-theme="light"] {
    --ink: #16181d; --ink-soft: #4a5160; --ink-faint: #767d8c;
    --rule: #d8dce4; --rule-soft: #e8ebf0; --bg: #ffffff; --panel: #f5f6f9;
    --accent: #1d4ed8; --accent-soft: #eef2ff;
    --warn-bg: #fdf6ec; --warn-rule: #e6d4b8;
  }

  body {
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Inter", -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .sheet {
    max-width: 8.1in;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 28px 30px 36px;
  }

  /* ---- header ---- */
  header {
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 21px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .sub {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 3px 0 0;
  }
  .total {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* ---- prep ---- */
  .prep {
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 11px 14px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .prep h2 {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  .prep ol {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 17px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .prep li { margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .prep li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* ---- phases ---- */
  .phase {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 62px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 13px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
  }
  .phase:first-of-type { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .clock {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--accent);
    padding-top: 1px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .clock span {
    display: block;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .phase h3 {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .phase p {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .phase p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .say {
    border-left: 2.5px solid var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    padding: 7px 11px;
    margin: 7px 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-radius: 0 3px 3px 0;
  }
  .say b {
    display: block;
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 9.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  .gate {
    border: 1px solid var(--warn-rule);
    background: var(--warn-bg);
    padding: 7px 11px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    margin-top: 7px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .gate b { font-weight: 700; }

  ul.prompts {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    padding-left: 0;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  ul.prompts li {
    padding: 2.5px 0 2.5px 15px;
    position: relative;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  ul.prompts li::before {
    content: "→";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  ul.prompts em { color: var(--ink); font-style: italic; }

  /* ---- troubleshooting ---- */
  .trouble {
    margin-top: 20px;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding-top: 12px;
  }
  .trouble h2 {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin: 0 0 9px;
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 8px 22px;
  }
  .fix {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .fix b {
    display: block;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .fix span { color: var(--ink-soft); }

  footer {
    margin-top: 16px;
    padding-top: 9px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .sheet { padding: 20px 16px 28px; }
    .phase { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
    .clock { padding-top: 0; }
    .clock span { display: inline; margin-left: 6px; }
    .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  /* ---- print: one page ---- */
  @page { size: letter portrait; margin: 0.45in; }
  @media print {
    :root {
      --ink: #000; --ink-soft: #2a2a2a; --ink-faint: #555;
      --rule: #999; --rule-soft: #ccc; --bg: #fff; --panel: #f2f2f2;
      --accent: #000; --accent-soft: #f0f0f0;
      --warn-bg: #f7f7f7; --warn-rule: #999;
    }
    body { font-size: 9.6pt; line-height: 1.32; }
    .sheet { max-width: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    header { margin-bottom: 9px; padding-bottom: 6px; }
    h1 { font-size: 15pt; }
    .sub { font-size: 8.6pt; }
    .total { font-size: 7.6pt; }
    .prep { margin-bottom: 9px; padding: 7px 9px; break-inside: avoid; }
    .prep ol { font-size: 8.8pt; }
    .phase { padding: 7px 0; gap: 11px; grid-template-columns: 54px 1fr; break-inside: avoid; }
    .phase h3 { font-size: 10.4pt; margin-bottom: 2px; }
    .phase p { font-size: 9.2pt; margin-bottom: 3px; }
    .clock { font-size: 9.6pt; }
    .clock span { font-size: 7.2pt; }
    .say { padding: 4px 8px; margin: 4px 0; font-size: 9pt; border-left-width: 2px; }
    .say b { font-size: 7pt; }
    .gate { padding: 4px 8px; font-size: 8.8pt; margin-top: 4px; }
    ul.prompts { font-size: 9pt; }
    ul.prompts li { padding: 1px 0 1px 13px; }
    .trouble { margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 8px; break-inside: avoid; }
    .grid { gap: 5px 18px; }
    .fix { font-size: 8.6pt; line-height: 1.32; }
    footer { margin-top: 9px; padding-top: 6px; font-size: 7.6pt; }
  }
</style>

<div class="sheet">

  <header>
    <div>
      <h1>Monday Reading Protocol</h1>
      <p class="sub">One hard passage — 2–3 paragraphs, not a whole section.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="total">27 min</div>
  </header>

  <div class="prep">
    <h2>Before class · 15 min</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Write, in one sentence, <b>the mechanism the passage explains</b>. If you can't, pick a different passage.</li>
      <li>Name its structure — most science text is a cause/effect chain or a process.</li>
      <li>Choose three self-explanation prompts from the list below.</li>
      <li>Decide the front-load: how will they get the idea <em>before</em> they read it?</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="phase">
    <div class="clock">0–8<span>Book shut</span></div>
    <div>
      <h3>Front-load the knowledge</h3>
      <p>Give them the phenomenon in plain language — demo, board sketch, short video, or just talk. No textbook vocabulary; if you must use a term, define it concretely on the spot.</p>
      <div class="say">
        <b>Say something like</b>
        "Here's what's going on. Water moves across the membrane toward wherever there's more dissolved stuff. That's it — that's the whole idea. Everything in the reading is a detail on top of that sentence."
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <b>Gate:</b> cold-call two students with <em>"What's this about?"</em> If they can't answer, spend three more minutes here. <b>Do not open the book yet.</b>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="phase">
    <div class="clock">8–10<span>Setup</span></div>
    <div>
      <h3>Name the structure out loud</h3>
      <p>Tell them the shape of the text and hand them a blank organizer that matches it.</p>
      <div class="say">
        <b>Say something like</b>
        "This passage is a chain — each thing causes the next. Your job is to find the links. Draw four boxes with arrows between them."
      </div>
      <p><b>Chain</b> → boxes + arrows &nbsp;·&nbsp; <b>Compare</b> → two columns &nbsp;·&nbsp; <b>Process</b> → numbered steps &nbsp;·&nbsp; <b>Claim/evidence</b> → claim box + bullets</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="phase">
    <div class="clock">10–22<span>Read</span></div>
    <div>
      <h3>Chunked read with written self-explanation</h3>
      <p>One paragraph at a time. Stop. One prompt, <b>in writing</b>, 60–90 seconds. Rotate prompts — never the same one twice. Take answers from two or three students between chunks. Correct mechanism errors; let awkward phrasing go.</p>
      <ul class="prompts">
        <li><em>"Say that in your own words. No textbook vocabulary allowed."</em></li>
        <li><em>"Why does that happen? What's the actual mechanism?"</em></li>
        <li><em>"What would break if that step didn't happen?"</em></li>
        <li><em>"How does that connect to the demo?"</em></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="phase">
    <div class="clock">22–27<span>Close</span></div>
    <div>
      <h3>Closed-book retrieval, then repair</h3>
      <div class="say">
        <b>Say exactly this</b>
        "Books shut. Two minutes — write everything you can about how this works." … then: "Open up. Different color pen. Mark what you missed and what you got wrong."
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <b>The repair step is non-negotiable.</b> Retrieval without checking can entrench errors. Never skip it for time — cut a paragraph instead.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="trouble">
    <h2>When it goes sideways</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="fix"><b>They can't self-explain at all</b><span>Front-load was too thin. Next time double it and cut a paragraph from the reading.</span></div>
      <div class="fix"><b>They write the textbook sentence back</b><span>The "no textbook vocabulary" rule isn't being enforced. Say it every single time.</span></div>
      <div class="fix"><b>It took 40 minutes, not 25</b><span>Normal on the first run. Cut to one paragraph, not three. Timings tighten fast.</span></div>
      <div class="fix"><b>The retrieval writing is blank</b><span>Don't panic or reteach on the spot. That's diagnostic information you didn't have before — that's the point.</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <footer>
    <b>Rollout:</b> weeks 1–2, front-load only. Weeks 3–4, add retrieval + repair. Month 2, run the full protocol on one hard passage per unit. Front-loading done every time beats the full protocol done occasionally.<br>
    <b>Note:</b> timings are calibrated to a 50-minute period, not derived from research. The underlying moves — build knowledge first, generate rather than reread, retrieve with feedback — rest on well-replicated findings; the specific dosage does not.
  </footer>

</div>
